Run records of codegen/c/bitwise_test.go's tests that build a program with clang flags
of their own and run it, written by tackc's porttest/rungen and completed
by tools/corpus --update; see tools/corpus/runs.tck for the format.
-- bitwise-example-runs/record --
replaces codegen/c/bitwise_test.go TestBitwiseExampleRuns/-O0
replaces codegen/c/bitwise_test.go TestBitwiseExampleRuns/-O1
replaces codegen/c/bitwise_test.go TestBitwiseExampleRuns/-O2
replaces codegen/c/bitwise_test.go TestBitwiseExampleRuns/-O3
strict-libs the test compiles its build's C with -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fstrict-flex-arrays=3 at its level and flags itself, which the driver's -w turns off; the runner compiles it so
dir examples/bitwise
opt 0 1 2 3
cflags -fstrict-flex-arrays=3 -fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE -ffinite-loops -mllvm -indvars-predicate-loops=true
lacks stdout "FAIL"
count stdout 22 " ok\n"
exit 0
